                    </span>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-brand-darkbrown">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                    <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-grey-muted">
                        Transparent clinical answers to common patient questions regarding braces, aligners, root canals, and appointments.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-3.5">
                    
                    <details class="group bg-brand-beige rounded-2xl border border-brand-border p-4 sm:p-5 transition-all">
                        <summary class="font-bold text-sm sm:text-base text-brand-darkbrown cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                            <span>Why should I choose an MDS Orthodontist instead of a general dentist for braces or clear aligners?</span>
                            <span class="text-brand-brown transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 font-bold">▾</span>
                        </summary>
                        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-grey-text mt-3 leading-relaxed border-t border-brand-border pt-3">
                            An Orthodontist is a dental surgeon who has undergone three years of dedicated post-graduate master residency (MDS) in facial aesthetics, craniofacial growth, and orthodontic biomechanics. While general dentists can order aligner kits, an MDS Orthodontist diagnoses the underlying bone support, prevents root damage, avoids facial profile flattening, and ensures your bite is stable for life.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="group bg-brand-beige rounded-2xl border border-brand-border p-4 sm:p-5 transition-all">
                        <summary class="font-bold text-sm sm:text-base text-brand-darkbrown cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                            <span>How much do braces and clear aligners cost in Kandivali West, and how long does treatment take?</span>
                            <span class="text-brand-brown transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 font-bold">▾</span>
                        </summary>
                        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-grey-text mt-3 leading-relaxed border-t border-brand-border pt-3">
                            Cost and timeline depend on dental crowding severity, skeletal jaw balance, and whether you choose metal, ceramic, self-ligating brackets, or custom clear aligners. Treatment typically ranges from 6 to 18 months. During your clinical consultation and 3D intraoral scan, you receive an itemized, written roadmap with no hidden costs and flexible installment options.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="group bg-brand-beige rounded-2xl border border-brand-border p-4 sm:p-5 transition-all">
                        <summary class="font-bold text-sm sm:text-base text-brand-darkbrown cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                            <span>Is Root Canal Treatment (RCT) painful at Infinora Dental Care?</span>
                            <span class="text-brand-brown transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 font-bold">▾</span>
                        </summary>
                        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-grey-text mt-3 leading-relaxed border-t border-brand-border pt-3">
                            No. Modern root canal treatment at our clinic is virtually painless. We utilize computer-guided electronic apex locators, nickel-titanium rotary instrumentation, and profound topical numbing prior to local anesthesia. Most patients report feeling only mild vibration or pressure, with acute toothache resolved in a single comfortable visit.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="group bg-brand-beige rounded-2xl border border-brand-border p-4 sm:p-5 transition-all">
                        <summary class="font-bold text-sm sm:text-base text-brand-darkbrown cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                            <span>How can I verify the clinic and doctor's statutory registrations?</span>
                            <span class="text-brand-brown transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 font-bold">▾</span>
                        </summary>
                        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-grey-text mt-3 leading-relaxed border-t border-brand-border pt-3">
                            Dr. Riddhi Patel Shah is registered with the Maharashtra State Dental Council (MSDC Registration No: A-45674) and verified on the Indian Dental Association national registry. Infinora Dental Care holds national certifications under the National Health Authority's Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (Health Facility ID: IN2710085962, Healthcare Professional ID: 71-8554-8443-4346).
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="group bg-brand-beige rounded-2xl border border-brand-border p-4 sm:p-5 transition-all">
                        <summary class="font-bold text-sm sm:text-base text-brand-darkbrown cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                            <span>What are your clinic operating hours, and do you accept Sunday appointments?</span>
                            <span class="text-brand-brown transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 font-bold">▾</span>
                        </summary>
                        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-grey-text mt-3 leading-relaxed border-t border-brand-border pt-3">
                            We are open Monday through Saturday from 09:00 AM to 09:00 PM across three daily sessions: Morning (09:00 AM – 01:00 PM), Afternoon (03:00 PM – 05:00 PM), and Evening (06:00 PM – 09:00 PM). On Sundays, we are open exclusively from 10:00 AM to 01:00 PM on a strictly prior appointment basis.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="group bg-brand-beige rounded-2xl border border-brand-border p-4 sm:p-5 transition-all">
                        <summary class="font-bold text-sm sm:text-base text-brand-darkbrown cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                            <span>Do you provide emergency dental services in Kandivali West?</span>
                            <span class="text-brand-brown transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 font-bold">▾</span>
                        </summary>
                        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-grey-text mt-3 leading-relaxed border-t border-brand-border pt-3">
                            Yes. We handle dental emergencies, including severe throbbing toothaches, sports trauma, broken or chipped teeth, dislodged brackets, poking orthodontic wires, and dental abscesses. Call our clinic desk directly at +91 73044 32681 for immediate triage and same-day scheduling.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="group bg-brand-beige rounded-2xl border border-brand-border p-4 sm:p-5 transition-all">
                        <summary class="font-bold text-sm sm:text-base text-brand-darkbrown cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                            <span>At what age should my child have their first orthodontic screening?</span>
                            <span class="text-brand-brown transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 font-bold">▾</span>
                        </summary>
                        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-grey-text mt-3 leading-relaxed border-t border-brand-border pt-3">
                            Both the Indian Orthodontic Society and international associations recommend a child's first orthodontic evaluation by age 7. At this developmental stage, permanent first molars have erupted, allowing an orthodontist to detect narrow arches, crossbites, thumb-sucking distortions, or jaw imbalances early—preventing invasive extractions or surgeries later in life.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="group bg-brand-beige rounded-2xl border border-brand-border p-4 sm:p-5 transition-all">
                        <summary class="font-bold text-sm sm:text-base text-brand-darkbrown cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                            <span>What payment methods and installment options are available?</span>
                            <span class="text-brand-brown transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 font-bold">▾</span>
                        </summary>
                        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-grey-text mt-3 leading-relaxed border-t border-brand-border pt-3">
                            We accept Cash, UPI (Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm), Debit Cards, Credit Cards, Mobile Tap NFC, and Bank Transfers. For comprehensive procedures such as clear aligners, complex braces, dental implants, or full-mouth smile makeovers, we provide structured stage-wise payment schedules and flexible EMI options.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                </div>
            </div>
